## Authentication
Authorization Header — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (3)
- `GET /front-static/nosey/fall/{fallToken}` — Complete authentication flow using a fall token.
- `GET /front-static/pages/home/fall/hero/{heroToken}` — Complete authentication flow using a hero token.
- `POST /sessions/{sessionId}` — Manage or update an existing user session.

### Data Read (4)
- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve data associated with a specific ID.
- `GET /cm/{cmId}/translations/en.json` — Retrieve English translations for a content module.
- `GET /front-api/notifications/en-US` — Get user notifications in English (US).
- `GET /organizations/{organizationId}/routing` — Get routing information for an organization.

### Data Write (2)
- `POST /traffic` — Submit traffic data for analysis.
- `POST /webevents/visitWebPage` — Record a user's visit to a specific web page.

### Media (1)
- `GET /_next/image` — Retrieve an image from the _next image service.

### Core API (3)
- `POST /api/v3/etClient` — Execute a core API function via the etClient endpoint.
- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Execute a core API function using a v1 ID.
- `POST /wa/` — Execute a core API function via the /wa/ endpoint.

## Quick Start

Here are a few examples to get you started using the `notion-so` API:

```typescript
// Example: Retrieving data associated with a specific ID.
// Assumes you have a valid ID.
async function getData(id: string) {
  try {
    const data = await client.getById(id);
    console.log("Data:", data);
    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error retrieving data:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
